{"key":"enterprise/T1071.003","id":"T1071.003","name":"Mail Protocols","domain":"enterprise","level":"subtechnique","parent_id":"T1071","tactics":["command-and-control"],"platforms":["Linux","macOS","Network Devices","Windows"],"environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","network-infrastructure","onprem"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may communicate using application layer protocols associated with electronic mail delivery to avoid detection/network filtering by blending in with existing traffic. Commands to the remote system, and often the results of those commands, will be embedded within the protocol traffic between the client and server. Protocols such as SMTP/S, POP3/S, and IMAP that carry electronic mail may be very common in environments. Packets produced…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1071/003","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--54b4c251-1f0e-4eba-ba6b-dbc7a6f6f06b","source_modified":"2025-10-24T17:48:48.564Z","source_object_version":"1.2","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0082","name":"Network Connection Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0082","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--181a9f8c-c780-4f1f-91a8-edb770e904ba","page":"telemetry/DC0082/"},{"id":"DC0085","name":"Network Traffic Content","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0085","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3772e279-27d6-477a-9fe3-c6beb363594c","page":"telemetry/DC0085/"},{"id":"DC0078","name":"Network Traffic Flow","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0078","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--a7f22107-02e5-4982-9067-6625d4a1765a","page":"telemetry/DC0078/"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0032","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3d20385b-24ef-40e1-9f56-f39750379077","page":"telemetry/DC0032/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0135","name":"Detection of Mail Protocol-Based C2 Activity (SMTP, IMAP, POP3)","url"